ctions associated with these agents are clinically significant. 鲑降钙素 can cause neurological side effects such as 肱晕 (dizziness) and tinnitus, warranting discontinuation if they occur [Data: Relationships (17399); Entities (16975)]. Additionally, because salmon calcitonin is a polypeptide, it poses a risk of systemic allergic reactions, particularly in atopic individuals, necessitating pre-treatment skin testing [Data: Relationships (17400); Entities (15512)]. Meanwhile, 复方雌孕 is linked to long-term risks including breast cancer and adverse lipid changes, which may increase cardiovascular risk [Data: Relationships (10774, 10775, 10778)]. These safety concerns require thorough risk-benefit discussions before prescribing.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Drug-drug interactions may compromise therapeutic efficacy\",\n            \"explanation\": \"复方雌孕 exhibits a clinically relevant interaction with 安鲁米特 (aminoglutethimide), an aromatase inhibitor used in hormone-sensitive cancers. Co-administration significantly reduces the bioavailability of medroxyprogesterone acetate (MPA), a common progestin component in combination therapies [Data: Relationships (34949); Entities (5110, 4786)]. This interaction could undermine the endometrial protective effect of progestin in estrogen-based regimens, increasing the risk of endometrial hyperplasia or cancer in women with a uterus. Clinicians must evaluate concomitant medications to avoid unintended therapeutic failure.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"The community reflects a focused therapeutic domain centered on hormonal and bone metabolism regulation\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The entities and relationships form a tightly interconnected network focused on postmenopausal health, osteoporosis management, and calcium homeostasis. Key diseases include绝经后骨质疏松症, 老年性骨质疏松症, 继发性骨质疏松症, and 高钙危象, all linked to either 复方雌孕 or 鲑降钙素 formulations [Data: Entities (1802, 1862, 1814, 2711); Relations